.TH DWM 1 dwm\-VERSION
.SH NAME
dwm \- dynamic window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwm
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
dwm is a dynamic window manager for X. It manages windows in tiled, monocle
and floating layouts. Either layout can be applied dynamically, optimising the
environment for the application in use and the task performed.
.P
In tiled layouts windows are managed in a master and stacking area. The master
area on the left contains one window by default, and the stacking area on the
right contains all other windows. the master area can be toggled on or off. In monocle layout all windows are
maximised to the screen size. In floating layout windows can be resized and
moved freely. Dialog windows are always managed floating, regardless of the
layout applied.
.P
Windows are grouped by tags. Each window can be tagged with one or multiple
tags. Selecting certain tags displays all windows with these tags.
.P
Each screen contains a small status bar which displays all available tags, the
layout, the titles of windows on the current desktop, and the text read from the root window
name property, if the screen is focused. A floating window is indicated with an
empty square and a maximised floating window is indicated with a filled square
before the windows title.  The selected tags are indicated with a different
color. The tags of the focused window are indicated with a filled square in the
top left corner.  The tags which are applied to one or more windows are
indicated with an empty square in the top left corner.
.P
dwm draws a small border around windows to indicate the focus state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
prints version information to stderr, then exits.
.SH USAGE
.SS Status bar
.TP
.B X root window name
is read and displayed in the status text area. It can be set with the
.BR xsetroot (1)
command.
.TP
.B Button1
click on a tag label to display all windows with that tag, click on the layout
label toggles between tiled and floating layout.
.TP
.B Button3
click on a tag label adds/removes all windows with that tag to/from the view.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button1
click on a tag label applies that tag to the focused window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button3
click on a tag label adds/removes that tag to/from the focused window.
.SS keyboard commands
Mod4 is the super/meta key.
.TP
.B Mod4, Alt\-F1, Mod4\-space
open the launcher.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Return
open st.
.TP
.B Mod4\-b/c/x/p/z/f
open firefox, code, discord, keepassxc, spotify or dolphin.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-c/r/y
run the color picker, recorder or screenshot helper.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-q
close the selected window.
.TP
.B Alt\-Tab, Alt\-Shift\-Tab
cycle windows; release alt to select or escape to cancel.
.TP
.B Alt\-grave, Alt\-Shift\-grave
cycle windows of the current application.
.TP
.B Mod4\-[1..4], Mod4\-Shift\-[1..4]
switch desktop or move the selected window to a desktop.
.TP
.B Mod4\-arrows
snap to a half screen; repeat to restore.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Alt\-arrows
focus a window in the given direction.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Prior, Mod4\-Next, Mod4\-Shift\-Next
maximize, minimize or restore a minimized window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-d, Control\-F12
show or restore the desktop on the current monitor.
.TP
.B Mod4\-w, Control\-F10, Control\-F9
list all windows, or current desktop windows with f9; enter selects, escape cancels.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-Left/Right
move the selected window to another monitor.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-Shift\-Left/Right
move the selected window to an adjacent desktop.
.TP
.B Mod4\-l, Mod4\-v
lock the screen or open clipboard history; external helpers are required.
.TP
.B Control\-Alt\-Delete
show the logout confirmation menu.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-j/k/h/l/i/Return
focus next/previous, adjust master width, toggle master area, or promote a window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-t/f/m/space/b/F11
select tile/float/monocle, toggle floating, toggle bar, or toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-c, Mod4\-Control\-Shift\-c
cycle accent colors forward or backward.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-comma/period
focus the previous or next monitor.
.SS Mouse commands
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button1
Move focused window while dragging. Tiled windows will be toggled to the floating state.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button2
Toggles focused window between floating and tiled state.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button3
Resize focused window while dragging. Tiled windows will be toggled to the floating state.
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
edit config.def.h and rebuild. config.h is generated by make.
README.local.md documents the full mapping and session setup.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dmenu (1),
.BR st (1)
.SH ISSUES
Java applications which use the XToolkit/XAWT backend may draw grey windows
only. The XToolkit/XAWT backend breaks ICCCM-compliance in recent JDK 1.5 and early
JDK 1.6 versions, because it assumes a reparenting window manager. Possible workarounds
are using JDK 1.4 (which doesn't contain the XToolkit/XAWT backend) or setting the
environment variable
.BR AWT_TOOLKIT=MToolkit
(to use the older Motif backend instead) or running
.B xprop -root -f _NET_WM_NAME 32a -set _NET_WM_NAME LG3D
or
.B wmname LG3D
(to pretend that a non-reparenting window manager is running that the
XToolkit/XAWT backend can recognize) or when using OpenJDK setting the environment variable
.BR _JAVA_AWT_WM_NONREPARENTING=1 .
.SH BUGS
See README.md for project details and upstream credits.
